# Shell scripts and the docker config they source MUST be LF, whatever the checkout platform does.
# A CRLF entrypoint.sh makes the container fail at exec with the famously unhelpful
# "exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" — the kernel is reporting that
# "/bin/bash\r" does not exist, not the script. Observed 2026-08-10 on a Windows checkout.
*.sh            text eol=lf
docker/**       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf

# The compose files and the LiteLLM proxy config are consumed INSIDE Linux
# containers, and docker-compose.test.yml now embeds a /bin/sh entrypoint
# script (the litellm config template render). A CRLF checkout puts \r into
# that script and it fails the same way a CRLF entrypoint.sh does -- see the
# note above. config.yaml is bind-mounted and sed-rendered, so it needs the
# same guarantee. Added 2026-09-14 with the llmproxy profile.
docker-compose*.yml  text eol=lf
litellm/**           text eol=lf
